# Vibration (added 2026-10-04). The aw8697 haptic driver plays every vibration
# from a waveform file: a request of N ms (from hfd-service) loads
# firmware/<N rounded to 20>ms_RTP.bin, and anything over 500 ms loops
# 500ms_RTP.bin. Without them the motor never moves (kernel log:
# "aw8697_rtp_work_routine: failed to read 300ms_RTP.bin").
# aw8697_haptic_170.bin is the chip's RAM waveform library. It also sets
# ram.base_addr, the RTP FIFO chunk size: without it the driver starts RTP
# playback, writes 0 bytes and the chip stays in RTP mode for good, after
# which every later vibration is ignored ("rtp_going" stays 1).
firmware/aw8697_haptic_170.bin
firmware/20ms_RTP.bin
firmware/40ms_RTP.bin
firmware/60ms_RTP.bin
firmware/80ms_RTP.bin
firmware/100ms_RTP.bin
firmware/120ms_RTP.bin
firmware/140ms_RTP.bin
firmware/160ms_RTP.bin
firmware/180ms_RTP.bin
firmware/200ms_RTP.bin
firmware/220ms_RTP.bin
firmware/240ms_RTP.bin
firmware/260ms_RTP.bin
firmware/280ms_RTP.bin
firmware/300ms_RTP.bin
firmware/320ms_RTP.bin
